criteria.notes:
SEC-R-1 half: met. The limiter fails open only for GET and HEAD and only on a busy error. Reads wait at most 50 ms, and the busy timeout is restored in a finally block. A call with no method fails closed. The hook passes the method, logger and request id. All of it is mutant-tested (L1-L5, R1), and P1 shows it end to end.

FU-23 half: not met for upgraded databases (SEC-RW4-1). Everything else in 006 holds:
- staging covers every CASCADE child, and no child uses SET NULL or RESTRICT;
- foreign-key checks are deferred to COMMIT, and rollback is atomic;
- indexes and triggers are byte-identical, and the schema equals a fresh one;
- the SET NULL choice is sound, because gate.js sums by day and customer only.
The RS-39 tests and migrate-006 delete only after migrating (migrate-006 L164-L178), so they cannot see the reuse of ids deleted before the upgrade.
